worksuite-os (1.0.0~dev3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Drivers (#69): a Debian mirror other than deb.debian.org and
    security.debian.org is approved only when it is pinned to Debian's
    archive keyring; other *.debian.org hosts with their own key
    (people.debian.org) are refused like any third-party archive.

 -- WorkSuite OS Team <os@worksuitecloud.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

worksuite-os (1.0.0~dev2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Drivers (#69): Debian's own APT sources are recognised (deb822 embedded
    Signed-By keys, *.debian.org mirrors, mirrors pinned to Debian's archive
    keyring, http/https duplicates, installation-disc entries); unsigned
    Debian lines get Debian's keyring; trusted=yes and missing Signed-By
    keyrings are refused by name. Settings › Drivers names the failed stage
    and the source, offers Try again, and asks for a restart only after a
    successful install that needs one.
  * Security (#68): Quick scan / Full scan say why they can't start in the
    engine's real state (definitions still downloading, updater failed or not
    installed, engine not responding, or the agent's own code); a stopped
    freshclam is started when a scan is asked for; Settings names why
    automatic updates aren't running and offers Update definitions; the image
    creates /var/lib/clamav and /var/log/clamav for clamav at boot.
  * Shell (#70): the taskbar's Accessibility panel uses the design-system
    pieces: Display and Language groups, the Settings switch with On/Off,
    a segmented text-size control (radio group, arrow keys), a full-width
    language picker, theme variables and rem sizes so it scales.

 -- WorkSuite OS Team <os@worksuitecloud.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000

